/// Associates a resource with the feed. The resource provides the input
/// that Elemental Inference needs in order to perform an Elemental
/// Inference feature, such as cropping video. You always provide the
/// resource by associating it with a feed. You can associate only one
/// resource with each feed. With an association, a specific source media is
/// claiming ownership of the feed. AssociateFeed is a PATCH operation,
/// which means that you can include only parameters that you want to
/// change. Parameters that you don't include will not be affected by the
/// operation. Specifically: You can add more outputs to the existing
/// outputs. New outputs will be appended. You can't modify an existing
/// output (for example to change its name). Instead, use UpdateFeed. You
/// can't delete an existing output. Instead, use UpdateFeed. Also note that
/// you can't change the feed name with AssociateFeed. Instead, use
/// UpdateFeed.
pub fn (c: Client) associate_feed(input: AssociateFeedRequest) -> AssociateFeedResponse ! AssociateFeedErr uses (net.dial, clock, rand) {
  let (ep, signing, extra) = c.route(endpoint_params_associate_feed(c.params, input)) ?? e => return Err(AssociateFeedErr.InvalidInput(e))
  var req = serialize_associate_feed(ep, input, rest.uuid(c.rand)) ?? e => return Err(AssociateFeedErr.InvalidInput(e))
  for h in extra {
    req.headers.push(h)
  }
  let resp = transport.send(c.transport, req, signing, restjson.classify) ?? e => return Err(AssociateFeedErr.Send(e))
  if resp.status >= 300 {
    return Err(deserialize_associate_feed_error(resp))
  }
  deserialize_associate_feed(resp) ?? e => Err(AssociateFeedErr.Deserialize(e))
}

